  "known_limitations": {
    "no-top-k-diversity": "adv-crowding-01: five near-identical dailies take all five slots and the note holding the conclusion does not appear. Top-K selection does not consider redundancy.",
    "expansion-reintroduces-ambiguity": "adv-ambiguity-01/02/03: 代理 is in AMBIGUOUS_TERMS and expands into both the agent and proxy concepts. adv-ambiguity-03 shows this is not only a query-time problem: the unambiguous 智能体 expands to 代理, which then matches 反向代理 in the other reading.",
    "term-overlap-is-treated-as-evidence": "every no-answer case returns hits. A query sharing one strong term with a note produces that note, with no notion of insufficient evidence. The stable corpus scores 1.0 here because its no-answer queries share nothing with any note.",
    "title-weight-outranks-the-answer": "adv-field-01/03: a stub whose title matches ranks above the note that answers the question. FIELD_WEIGHTS[title] is 6x body.",
    "section-length-normalisation": "adv-dilution-01: section-level ranking (#118) brings the sectioned 75 KB note into Top-5 at rank 2 and leaves the unstructured one absent, which is the measurement working — a section can compete on its own evidence only where sections exist. What remains is that the unstructured shape has no remedy here at all: one heading means one passage, and no split can help it. adv-dilution-05 still returns a short note that names the terms and says it does not cover them, above the section that answers, because term overlap is still treated as evidence — see below."
  },
